  "title": "Nikon QV-1000C Still Video Camera System",
  "year": "1988",
  "subtitle": "Shoot to a floppy disk, pop it into a transmitter, clamp on the acoustic coupler, and phone your photo across the country in minutes.",
  "why_scout_cares": "The QV-1000C is an entire photojournalism workflow compressed into a shoulder bag: a filmless camera writing stills to a reusable 2-inch magnetic floppy disk, a transmission unit that dials out over a phone line, and an acoustic-coupler ritual to shove the picture across the wire. Before mobile data existed, this is how a photo raced from a remote assignment to a newsroom. A full embodied chain of camera, disk, transmitter, coupler and phone.",
  "search_terms": ["Nikon QV-1000C", "Nikon QV1000C", "still video camera", "S-VHS video floppy", "QT-1000C transmitter", "acoustic coupler photojournalism", "Nikon filmless 1988"],
